/stata_gen_yaml contains the Stata program tree that turns spreadsheet data into YAML files. 

See /Documentation/DMC YAML Generation Pipeline for a visualization of the data pipeline.

/Derived/ contains the file produced by the Stata tree that is used as the input for auto-generated YAML code

/Documentation/ contains critical input files

/Output/ contains YAML code produced by the tree. It has subfolders for each cohort, which in turn each contain subfolders titled "good", "bad", & "fixed"

/Programs/ contains the Stata programs

/Raw/ contains spreadsheets of metadata exported from dbGAP

/temp/ is a directory for intermediate files produced when the Stata program tree runs. These are not necessary to retain, but can aid in troubleshooting if the program tree breaks.